A||N||8||Daleford||Getrag recognition||||5||
Z||000000||Daleford||12-21-2000||11:34 AM||||Will I know you when I find you?  Looking for a 5-speed Getrag from a 86-88 Fiero. I know how to check out the Fiero's serial number to confirm, but if the transaxel is sitting on a salvage yard floor, how do I know it is the real thing?  Any nunbers, distinguishing features, photos anyone?  Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||12-21-2000||01:19 PM||||I don't know how to tell the difference from a Fiero or non-Fiero Getrag, but If you know it is from a Fiero, I think only the Getrag has the dipstick in the case.  <P>The Chilton's manual has some drawings of the different transmissions since they cover some trans. maintenance.  You should be able to see the difference in the cases and how the shift linkage connects.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||12-21-2000||04:30 PM||||The small Chilton's manual has the pictures labeled incorrectly, so be carefull with that. Also, I have seen (with my own eyes) a four speed with a dip-stick, so the Getrag is not the only one that has a dip-stick. <P>The Getrag has a flat steel cover plate bolted on the left side of the case (the end opposite the engine pulleys). That's what I look for. The Isuzus have a cast aluminum cover.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000003||ur2biteme||12-22-2000||04:06 AM||||and the isuzu's dont have a dipstick.  you check the fluid by pulling the VSS and checking the marks on it. <P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mark||12-22-2000||07:41 AM||||Does the VIN appear anywhere on the transaxle?  That would be a dead giveaway.||||reg||1
Z||000005||JetroGT||12-22-2000||07:56 AM||||I thought that only the 88's had the dip sitick on the manual tranny.||||reg||5
Z||000006||StuGood||12-22-2000||01:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>...The Getrag has a flat steel cover plate bolted on the left side of the case (the end opposite the engine pulleys). That's what I look for. The Isuzus have a cast aluminum cover.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sounds like it'd be a good idea to bring Mr. Magnet with you, to the salvage yard  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000007||Hawk||12-22-2000||02:02 PM||||87 getrag trannys have a dip stick on the top||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||12-25-2000||05:24 AM||||my 86 Getrag has a screw-in dipstick.  I didn't think the 4-speeds had dipsticks?||||reg||1
